{{!
    @template mod_syllabus/narrative_field

    One editable narrative Custom Field box, shared by the plan/week/activity editable
    loops. When the author's preferred editor is Tiny (tinyavailable — resolved once at the
    top of tab_full_plan's render and read here via Mustache's normal context-stack
    fallback), the field starts as a focusable, formatted read-only preview styled to look
    like an open text field — no separate "Edit" button or read/edit mode switch to notice.
    Focusing it (click or Tab) lazily attaches a full Tiny instance in its place
    (amd/src/narrative_editor.js) and removes it again on blur, so a page with many
    narrative fields never has more than a couple of live editor instances at once — the
    user only ever sees "a text box that becomes rich when you click into it". A user whose
    own editor preference is the plain textarea (tinyavailable false) gets exactly that,
    unchanged, with no lazy-load machinery attached.

    The id/data-syllabus-section pair on the wrapper is harmless even for week/activity
    fields that have no matching rail entry — plan_navigator.js simply finds no link for
    that section id and does nothing.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "fieldid": 7,
        "instanceid": 2,
        "elementid": "syllabus-field-2-7",
        "name": "Details",
        "text": "<p>Some text.</p>",
        "itemid": 9,
        "area": "week",
        "isplanfield": false,
        "description": "Describe what happens in this week's class.",
        "tinyavailable": true
    }
}}
<div class="syllabus-field mb-3" id="syllabus-section-field-{{fieldid}}" data-syllabus-section>
    <h3><label id="{{elementid}}-label" for="{{elementid}}">{{name}}</label></h3>
    {{#description}}
    <p class="form-text text-muted syllabus-field-help">{{{description}}}</p>
    {{/description}}
    {{#tinyavailable}}
    <div class="syllabus-narrative-field">
        <div class="syllabus-narrative-preview" tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="{{elementid}}-label">{{{text}}}</div>
        <textarea id="{{elementid}}" class="syllabus-customfield-editor d-none{{#isplanfield}} syllabus-required-input{{/isplanfield}}"
            data-fieldid="{{fieldid}}" data-instanceid="{{instanceid}}" data-area="{{area}}"
            data-itemid="{{itemid}}">{{text}}</textarea>
    </div>
    {{/tinyavailable}}
    {{^tinyavailable}}
    <textarea id="{{elementid}}" class="syllabus-customfield-editor{{#isplanfield}} syllabus-required-input{{/isplanfield}}"
        data-fieldid="{{fieldid}}" data-instanceid="{{instanceid}}" data-area="{{area}}" data-itemid="{{itemid}}">{{text}}</textarea>
    {{/tinyavailable}}
    <span class="syllabus-save-status d-none small text-muted"
        data-saving="{{#str}} saving, mod_syllabus {{/str}}"
        data-saved="{{#str}} saved, mod_syllabus {{/str}}"></span>
</div>
